{"change_summary":"Updated the substrate redox implementation to count substrate-associated microfauna respiration in `estimate_substrate_o2_demand_rate`, switched the diffusion porosity approximation from a depth-weighted bed average to the first non-zero surface layer so shallow caps act as the O2 bottleneck, added regression tests for heterogeneous stacked substrates and microfauna-driven penetration shallowing, and wired the existing `shrimp_failed_molt_accum` snapshot field through snapshot construction/deserialization so the current worktree builds for validation.","outstanding_risks":["The heterogeneous-bed diffusion approximation is now surface-limited, but it is still a first-pass single-porosity model; a deeper low-porosity barrier below a porous cap would still need a piecewise resistance solve for full fidelity.","`cargo test -p tank_core` still fails in the current dirty worktree at `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs:309` (`molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes`), which is outside the substrate files changed here.","`cargo test -p tank_core` still emits an unrelated unused-import warning in `crates/tank_core/tests/source_water_carbonate.rs`."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect the current substrate-zone demand and porosity helpers, confirm where the stacked-bed diffusion bottleneck is computed, and review nearby regression coverage before editing.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Implement the substrate redox amendments by adding substrate-linked microfauna O2 demand, changing the porosity input to a surface-layer bottleneck approximation, and fixing snapshot initialization for the already-present failed-molt accumulator field so validation can build.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Add regression tests for microfauna-driven shallowing and heterogeneous surface-cap bottlenecks, then run formatting and focused/full validation to verify the change set.","order":2,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all`","`cargo test -p tank_core --lib substrate` passed (17/17 substrate unit tests, including the new heterogeneous-cap and microfauna-demand regressions).","`cargo test -p tank_core` ran successfully through the updated substrate and snapshot coverage, then failed later at `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs:309` (`molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes`) in unrelated dirty-worktree code.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test events molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes -- --nocapture` reproduced the unrelated event-test failure for isolation." ]}